      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just a fog though. it's more like... look at the logic of it. if universe is entropy and everything eventually ends and nothing we do has permanent impact, then the value of existence is effectively zero. if the net value is zero, then the choice to exist or not to exist is mathematically equal. i can't see how one is \"better\" than the other if they both result in nothingness. makes sense, right?\n Balance the equation if you equals zero.  mathematician",
